# Parking Lot Class Diagram

Below is the UML class diagram showing the connections, inheritance, and compositions of all the classes and interfaces within the `parkingLot` system. 

```mermaid
classDiagram
    %% Core Entities
    class ParkingLot {
        - static ParkingLot instance
        + List~ParkingFloor~ floors
        + List~EntranceGate~ entranceGates
        + List~ExitGate~ exitGates
        + FeeStrategy feeStrategy
        - ParkingLot()
        + static getInstance() ParkingLot
    }

    class ParkingFloor {
        + String floorId
        + List~ParkingSpot~ spots
        + ParkingFloor(String id)
    }

    class ParkingSpot {
        <<abstract>>
        + String id
        + boolean occupied
        + Vehicle vehicle
        + int distanceFromGate
        + ParkingSpot(String id, int distanceFromGate)
        + canFit(Vehicle vehicle)* boolean
        + isAvailable() boolean
        + park(Vehicle vehicle) void
        + release() void
    }

    class CarSpot
    class BikeSpot
    class TruckSpot

    class Vehicle {
        + String licensePlate
        + VehicleType type
        + Vehicle(String licensePlate, VehicleType type)
    }

    class VehicleType {
        <<enumeration>>
        CAR
        BIKE
        TRUCK
    }

    class Ticket {
        + String id
        + Vehicle vehicle
        + ParkingSpot spot
        + LocalDateTime entryTime
        - Ticket(TicketBuilder builder)
        + static builder() TicketBuilder
    }

    class TicketBuilder {
        - String id
        - Vehicle vehicle
        - ParkingSpot spot
        - LocalDateTime entryTime
        + id(String id) TicketBuilder
        + vehicle(Vehicle vehicle) TicketBuilder
        + spot(ParkingSpot spot) TicketBuilder
        + build() Ticket
    }

    %% Gates
    class EntranceGate {
        + String gateId
        + ParkingSpotLookupStrategy lookupStrategy
        + ParkingLot parkingLot
        + EntranceGate(String gateId, ParkingSpotLookupStrategy strategy)
        + parkVehicle(Vehicle vehicle) Ticket
    }

    class ExitGate {
        + String gateId
        + ParkingLot parkingLot
        + ExitGate(String gateId)
        + unparkVehicle(Ticket ticket) double
    }

    %% Strategies
    class FeeStrategy {
        <<interface>>
        + calculate(Ticket ticket) double
    }

    class HourlyFeeStrategy {
        + calculate(Ticket ticket) double
    }

    class ParkingSpotLookupStrategy {
        <<interface>>
        + findSpot(Vehicle vehicle, List~ParkingFloor~ floors) ParkingSpot
    }

    class NearestSpotStrategy {
        + findSpot(...) ParkingSpot
    }

    class FirstAvailableStrategy {
        + findSpot(...) ParkingSpot
    }

    %% Factories
    class ParkingSpotFactory {
        + static createSpot(VehicleType type, String id, int dist) ParkingSpot
    }

    class StrategyFactory {
        + static getLookupStrategy(String type) ParkingSpotLookupStrategy
        + static getFeeStrategy(String type) FeeStrategy
    }

    %% Relationships (Inheritance / Realization)
    ParkingSpot <|-- CarSpot
    ParkingSpot <|-- BikeSpot
    ParkingSpot <|-- TruckSpot
    
    FeeStrategy <|.. HourlyFeeStrategy
    ParkingSpotLookupStrategy <|.. NearestSpotStrategy
    ParkingSpotLookupStrategy <|.. FirstAvailableStrategy

    %% Relationships (Composition / Aggregation / Usage)
    ParkingLot --> ParkingFloor : contains
    ParkingLot --> EntranceGate : contains
    ParkingLot --> ExitGate : contains
    ParkingLot --> FeeStrategy : has default
    
    ParkingFloor o-- ParkingSpot : contains
    ParkingSpot o-- Vehicle : hosts
    Vehicle --> VehicleType : has
    
    Ticket *-- TicketBuilder : built by
    Ticket --> Vehicle : tracks
    Ticket --> ParkingSpot : assigned
    
    EntranceGate --> ParkingSpotLookupStrategy : uses
    EntranceGate --> Ticket : creates
    EntranceGate --> ParkingLot : references
    
    ExitGate --> ParkingLot : references
    ExitGate ..> Ticket : processes
    
    ParkingSpotFactory ..> ParkingSpot : creates
    StrategyFactory ..> FeeStrategy : creates
    StrategyFactory ..> ParkingSpotLookupStrategy : creates

```

### Diagram Explanations

1. **Inheritance & Implementation**: 
   - `CarSpot`, `BikeSpot`, and `TruckSpot` inherit from the abstract [ParkingSpot](file:///d:/System%20Design/LLD/Implementation/com/interviewQuestions/parkingLot/spots/ParkingSpot.java#5-32).
   - `HourlyFeeStrategy` implements the [FeeStrategy](file:///d:/System%20Design/LLD/Implementation/com/interviewQuestions/parkingLot/parkingStrategy/StrategyFactory.java#15-21) interface. 
   - `NearestSpotStrategy` and `FirstAvailableStrategy` implement the `ParkingSpotLookupStrategy` interface.
2. **Composition & Aggregation**: 
   - [ParkingLot](file:///d:/System%20Design/LLD/Implementation/com/interviewQuestions/parkingLot/entities/ParkingLot.java#10-30) aggregates `ParkingFloor`, [EntranceGate](file:///d:/System%20Design/LLD/Implementation/com/interviewQuestions/parkingLot/gates/EntranceGate.java#11-44), and [ExitGate](file:///d:/System%20Design/LLD/Implementation/com/interviewQuestions/parkingLot/gates/ExitGate.java#6-22).
   - [Ticket](file:///d:/System%20Design/LLD/Implementation/com/interviewQuestions/parkingLot/entities/Ticket.java#7-55) creates and uses its nested [TicketBuilder](file:///d:/System%20Design/LLD/Implementation/com/interviewQuestions/parkingLot/entities/Ticket.java#20-50) for instantiation.
3. **Usage via Factories**: 
   - [ParkingSpotFactory](file:///d:/System%20Design/LLD/Implementation/com/interviewQuestions/parkingLot/spots/ParkingSpotFactory.java#5-19) handles the logic to spawn specific Spot subclasses.
   - [StrategyFactory](file:///d:/System%20Design/LLD/Implementation/com/interviewQuestions/parkingLot/parkingStrategy/StrategyFactory.java#5-22) instantiates specific Strategy implementations. 
4. **Gates**: 
   - [EntranceGate](file:///d:/System%20Design/LLD/Implementation/com/interviewQuestions/parkingLot/gates/EntranceGate.java#11-44) coordinates finding the [ParkingSpot](file:///d:/System%20Design/LLD/Implementation/com/interviewQuestions/parkingLot/spots/ParkingSpot.java#5-32) via `ParkingSpotLookupStrategy` and issues a [Ticket](file:///d:/System%20Design/LLD/Implementation/com/interviewQuestions/parkingLot/entities/Ticket.java#7-55).
   - [ExitGate](file:///d:/System%20Design/LLD/Implementation/com/interviewQuestions/parkingLot/gates/ExitGate.java#6-22) leverages [ParkingLot](file:///d:/System%20Design/LLD/Implementation/com/interviewQuestions/parkingLot/entities/ParkingLot.java#10-30)'s [FeeStrategy](file:///d:/System%20Design/LLD/Implementation/com/interviewQuestions/parkingLot/parkingStrategy/StrategyFactory.java#15-21) context to evaluate the charge based on the given [Ticket](file:///d:/System%20Design/LLD/Implementation/com/interviewQuestions/parkingLot/entities/Ticket.java#7-55).
